100 HS_ADMIN 86400 1110 ADMIN 300::111111111111:0.NA/21.T11970
1 21.T11970/Type 86400 1110 UTF8 21.T11970/Profile
2 21.T11970/Profile 86400 1110 UTF8 21.T11970/AttributeDefSyntax
3 21.T11970/Data 86400 1110 UTF8 self
4 21.T11970/Name 86400 1110 UTF8 FDO_validation_strategy_for_combination
5 21.T11970/Description 86400 1110 UTF8 An attribute can use several validation mechanisms simultaneously. Which validation mechanism applies depends on the profile(s) used by the attribute definition: 21.T11970/AttributeDefSyntax, 21.T11970/AttributeDefComb, 21.T11970/AttributeDefUnion, 21.T11970/AttributeDefProfileRef, and 21.T11970/AttributeDefAttrRef. If several of these profiles are used by one attribute definition, 21.T11970/ValidationStrategyForCombination determines whether at least one validation mechanism must apply (anyof), or all of them (allof). The default is allof, in which case the attribute can be omitted.
6 21.T11970/Cardinality 86400 1110 UTF8 0..1
7 21.T11970/PrimitiveDataType 86400 1110 UTF8 string
8 21.T11970/Whitelist 86400 1110 UTF8 anyof
9 21.T11970/Whitelist 86400 1110 UTF8 allof

